t PAM armed for the whole lock, including while the displays are blank. Its second point (a flat 250 ms retry with no backoff spinning on hard device errors) no longer holds: upstream #7158 replaced it with a backoff. At this commit (upstream #7158 merged, which is in upstream quattro 035ce29f), the real Service.qml retry policy is: after an attempt that reached the reader and did not match, the next attempt is armed in 250 ms (FingerprintModel.js:3 and Service.qml:420 upstream); attempts that never reach the reader or end in a fast error back off 1, 2, 4 ... 32 s and then 40 s (FingerprintModel.js:7-23); runBlank() leaves a pending retry running (Service.qml:294-298) and a miss while the displays are blank arms the next attempt in 250 ms (startFingerprint, Service.qml:357-375, has no displaysBlank check); retries continue for as long as the session stays locked. SW-REQ-261004-296X covers the unavailable report and SW-REQ-260912-ND55 says the armed fingerprint PAM must not hold the display lit; no requirement says whether the reader is scanned while the displays are blank or whether retries have a total budget. That is an open specification question for the maintainers. Open upstream PRs #12420 and #7179 propose not scanning while blank. KI-LOCK-FPRINT-START-FAIL-NO-RETRY (fixed) was examined: the start-failure path, not this one.","validationDigest":"sha256:cb93aecbdce8f0edf0f4daf5a052c41cff78de5a410c2c18146a3206f77a2fd2","validationId":"rval-745154880ad90c47c99d5d68a7d1114c","verdict":"confirmed"}
